---
import '@fontsource/manrope/400.css';
import '@fontsource/manrope/500.css';
import '@fontsource/manrope/600.css';
import '@fontsource/manrope/700.css';
import '../../styles/global.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>The Unseen Details Inside a Car Deal | Smart Auto Buying</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="See how fees, add-ons, trade values, financing, and lease terms change the real shape of a car deal."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="guide-page premium-guide-page">
      <a class="guide-back" href="/#feature">Back to home</a>

      <article class="deal-article">
        <header class="deal-hero">
          <div class="deal-hero-copy">
            <p class="guide-kicker">Deal analysis</p>
            <h1>The unseen details inside a car deal</h1>
            <p class="guide-lede">
              Dealer quotes can hide the real story in fees, add-ons, trade values, financing, and
              lease terms. We help you read the numbers clearly before you make a move.
            </p>

            <div class="deal-meta">
              <div>
                <strong>4 layers</strong>
                <span>price, fees, trade, finance</span>
              </div>
              <div>
                <strong>1 decision</strong>
                <span>compare the full deal, not the pitch</span>
              </div>
              <div>
                <strong>0%</strong>
                <span>dealer commission pressure</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <figure class="deal-hero-image">
            <img
              src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1494976388531-d1058494cdd8?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1800&q=90"
              alt="A close-up of a luxury vehicle with a refined, high-end finish"
            />
          </figure>
        </header>

        <section class="deal-summary">
          <div class="deal-summary-copy">
            <h2>Why this page exists</h2>
            <p>
              A dealership quote can look simple at first glance, but the real story usually lives
              in the lines below the advertised payment. The point of this page is to separate the
              moving parts so you can make a decision with calm, not pressure.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="deal-summary-points">
            <div>
              <strong>Quote clarity</strong>
              <span>Identify which part of the deal is actually changing.</span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <strong>Negotiation leverage</strong>
              <span>Focus on the cost drivers that move the total.</span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <strong>Decision confidence</strong>
              <span>Understand the trade-offs before you sign.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="deal-chart-grid">
          <article class="deal-panel">
            <div class="deal-panel-heading">
              <p>Illustrative quote composition</p>
              <strong>$48,900 total</strong>
            </div>
            <div class="deal-donut-shell" aria-label="Illustrative quote breakdown chart">
              <div
                class="deal-donut"
                style="--vehicle: 71%; --fees: 15%; --addons: 9%; --finance: 5%;"
              ></div>
              <div class="deal-donut-copy">
                <h3>What the quote is made of</h3>
                <p>
                  This example shows how the vehicle price usually dominates the total, while fees,
                  add-ons, and finance terms still have enough weight to change the result.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="deal-legend">
              <div><span class="legend-swatch vehicle"></span><strong>Vehicle price</strong><em>71%</em></div>
              <div><span class="legend-swatch fees"></span><strong>Taxes and fees</strong><em>15%</em></div>
              <div><span class="legend-swatch addons"></span><strong>Add-ons</strong><em>9%</em></div>
              <div><span class="legend-swatch finance"></span><strong>Finance reserve</strong><em>5%</em></div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="deal-panel deal-panel-dark">
            <div class="deal-panel-heading">
              <p>Quote comparison</p>
              <strong>Three dealer offers</strong>
            </div>

            <div class="deal-bars" aria-label="Illustrative quote comparison chart">
              <div class="deal-bar-row">
                <div class="deal-bar-label">
                  <span>Dealer A</span>
                  <strong>$48,900</strong>
                </div>
                <div class="deal-bar-track"><span style="width: 100%"></span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="deal-bar-row">
                <div class="deal-bar-label">
                  <span>Dealer B</span>
                  <strong>$49,640</strong>
                </div>
                <div class="deal-bar-track"><span style="width: 93%"></span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="deal-bar-row">
                <div class="deal-bar-label">
                  <span>Dealer C</span>
                  <strong>$50,180</strong>
                </div>
                <div class="deal-bar-track"><span style="width: 88%"></span></div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <p class="deal-panel-note">
              Even a small difference in add-ons or financing can push the final figure well beyond
              the headline payment. That is why the full quote deserves a side-by-side read.
            </p>
          </article>
        </section>

        <section class="deal-matrix">
          <div class="deal-matrix-heading">
            <h2>The four things worth comparing every time</h2>
            <p>Use the same frame for every quote and the noise starts to drop away.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="deal-matrix-grid">
            <article>
              <strong>Price</strong>
              <span>Negotiate the vehicle number before any payment discussion.</span>
            </article>
            <article>
              <strong>Fees</strong>
              <span>Separate required government items from dealer-controlled charges.</span>
            </article>
            <article>
              <strong>Trade</strong>
              <span>Look at trade value and payoff as a standalone transaction.</span>
            </article>
            <article>
              <strong>Finance</strong>
              <span>Check rate, term, money factor, and any office products.</span>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <aside class="guide-callout premium-callout">
          <strong>Smart Auto Buying tip</strong>
          <p>
            Ask for the full buyer's order and compare each line item before discussing payment.
            That is usually where the clearest leverage lives.
          </p>
        </aside>
      </article>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
